# Origins allowed to appear inside a shipped artifact.
#
# Format:  <package or file prefix> | <license> | <why it is acceptable>
#
# The rule from CLAUDE.md §8: permissive (0BSD/MIT/BSD/Apache-2.0/EPL/MPL) or copyleft
# WITH a classpath/linking exception. Copyleft without one does not belong in a shipped
# artifact and must not be added here to make the check pass.
#
# This file is deliberately short. If checking an APK produces a wall of NOT ALLOWED
# lines, that is the current, real state of the Android build. See docs/LICENSE-AUDIT.md.
# Do not silence it by pasting the offenders in; that decision is the user's.

com.modcritic          | 0BSD                        | Our own code. See LICENSE.
javafx                 | GPLv2 + Classpath Exception | OpenJFX. The CE is what permits shipping our own code under 0BSD.
com.sun.javafx         | GPLv2 + Classpath Exception | OpenJFX internals, same artifact.
com.sun.glass          | GPLv2 + Classpath Exception | OpenJFX internals, same artifact.
com.sun.prism          | GPLv2 + Classpath Exception | OpenJFX internals, same artifact.
com.sun.scenario       | GPLv2 + Classpath Exception | OpenJFX internals, same artifact.
com.sun.marlin         | GPLv2 + Classpath Exception | OpenJFX's antialiasing rasterizer, in javafx-graphics.
com.sun.pisces         | GPLv2 + Classpath Exception | OpenJFX's older rasterizer, in javafx-graphics.
com.sun.openpisces     | GPLv2 + Classpath Exception | OpenJFX's older rasterizer, in javafx-graphics.
com.sun.util           | GPLv2 + Classpath Exception | Verified to come from javafx-graphics-21-<platform>.jar, not the JDK.

# Fonts ship inside the jar and the APK. OFL-1.1 requires the license text to travel
# with them, which is why OFL.txt is packaged beside them. See MANUAL.md's asset table.
NotoSansMono           | OFL-1.1                     | The interface typeface (D-6).
NotoSansMath           | OFL-1.1                     | Two glyphs Noto Sans Mono lacks.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Android only. None of these was chosen by anyone here; the Android build adds them.
# They were unrecorded until the M6.5a audit found them. All Apache-2.0, each confirmed
# from a <licenses> block on disk rather than assumed. See docs/LICENSE-AUDIT.md.

androidx                | Apache-2.0 | Pulled in by the generated Android project.
android.support         | Apache-2.0 | Legacy-named AIDL stubs living inside androidx core, not a separate library.
kotlin                  | Apache-2.0 | Kotlin standard library 2.0.21, required by androidx. No Kotlin is written here.
kotlinx                 | Apache-2.0 | Coroutines 1.8.1, same reason.
_COROUTINE              | Apache-2.0 | Marker classes the Kotlin coroutines library generates for stack traces.
org.jetbrains           | Apache-2.0 | JetBrains annotations, pulled in by Kotlin.
org.intellij            | Apache-2.0 | Same package family, same reason.
org.jspecify            | Apache-2.0 | Nullness annotations, pulled in by androidx.
com.google.common       | Apache-2.0 | Guava's listenablefuture stub only, pulled in transitively.

# The one native library we produce. Since M6.5b it contains our own host layer (0BSD),
# OpenJFX (GPLv2 + Classpath Exception), the GraalVM CE runtime (GPLv2 + Classpath
# Exception) and libc++ (Apache-2.0 with the LLVM exception), and nothing from Gluon.
libsubstrate.so         | mixed, all cleared | Verified per-component in docs/LICENSE-AUDIT.md section 4.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# STILL NOT LISTED, ON PURPOSE:
#
#   libfreetype.so   FreeType is dual licensed, FTL or GPLv2, and the choice is the
#                    distributor's. The copy shipped here is stripped, no license file
#                    exists anywhere on this machine, and the JavaFX SDK's own
#                    ADDITIONAL_LICENSE_INFO says only that FreeType "may" be included
#                    and is licensed "under their original licenses". Under FTL it is
#                    permissive with an attribution requirement and would be fine.
#                    Nobody has confirmed that from a file, so it stays off the list and
#                    the check stays red until someone does.
